## 5. Long-Term Architectural Alignment

- Every change must fit the project's long-term architecture: respect layer
  boundaries (UI ↔ `src/services/api.ts` ↔ NestJS services ↔ Prisma read / file
  store) exactly as the project draws them.
- New modules mirror the structure of the best existing module of the same kind.
- Cross-cutting concerns (logging, auth, error handling, notifications) go
  through the project's existing mechanisms — never a one-off implementation.
- When the user requests something architecturally significant (new module,
  schema redesign, integration), first present how it maps onto the existing
  architecture and get approval before writing code.

